# Workflow Standards

Thin hub for development workflow, code review, and process requirements. Domain detail lives in child rules — do not duplicate here.

**Maintenance:** Never re-grow this file with domain bodies (git, agent behavior, platform, etc.). Extract new concerns to a sibling `.cursor/rules/<category>/RULE.mdc` and add one row to § Rule routing.

## Rule routing

| Concern | SSOT |
|---------|------|
| Branch model, PRs, promote, commit/push flow | `git-workflow/RULE.mdc` |
| Protected files, decision protocol, success reporting (verified vs unverified) | `agent-behavior/RULE.mdc` |
| PowerShell, env vars, shell crash prevention | `platform/RULE.mdc` |
| Semver, changelog, commit format | `git-workflow/RULE.mdc` § Mode behavior table → **version source** (A/B: `.agents/skills/finish/SKILL.md`; C: release-please) |
| Reductive strategy / debugging | `debugging/RULE.mdc` |
| API doc research | `api-integration/RULE.mdc` |

## Branch gate (minimal)

Read `src/config/git-workflow.json`, then apply `.cursor/rules/git-workflow/RULE.mdc` § Mode-aware branch gate. Do not infer mode from the current branch.

