## Code Review Process

### Review Checklist
- [ ] Version and changelog per `git-workflow/RULE.mdc` § Mode behavior table → **version source** (A/B: changelog updated for user-facing changes and matches the `[VERSION]`-first commit message — `finish/SKILL.md`; C: conventional PR title, release-please does the rest)
- [ ] Code follows style guidelines (`code-style/RULE.mdc`)
- [ ] Architecture patterns are followed (`architecture/RULE.mdc`)
- [ ] Architecture documentation updated (if structural changes)
- [ ] Tests are included and passing (`testing/RULE.mdc`)
- [ ] Security considerations addressed (`security/RULE.mdc`)
- [ ] Documentation changes are limited to required contract docs only
- [ ] Feature-local README updated when `src/features/*` code changed
- [ ] No console.log or debug code left behind
- [ ] Linting passes (GTS or project-specified tool)

### Review Focus Areas
- Functionality, code quality, performance, security, testing

## Development Process

### Before Starting Work
- Understand requirements clearly; check existing patterns; plan before coding

### During Development

**Agents:** Commit timing per `git-workflow/RULE.mdc` § Mode behavior table → **commit timing** (A/B: never during `plan` or `implement` — commits happen in **`finish`** only; C: when the user asks, directly or via `finish`).

**Humans:** May commit frequently on the branch allowed by the current git-workflow mode (`src/config/git-workflow.json`); still use `finish` when agents wrap up work.

- Write tests per `testing/RULE.mdc` § When to use TDD / What to Test
- Refactor as you go; follow established patterns

### Before Submitting

- Changelog and version sync: per **version source** row (A/B: **`finish/SKILL.md`**, not during plan/implement; C: release-please)
- Run linters and tests; review your own code
- Update only required docs: `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `src/features/*/README.md`, and `CHANGELOG.md` when the **version source** row says `finish`
- Do not create new docs by default; deep docs need explicit user approval
- If feature code changed: stage README updates and run `pnpm validate:feature-docs:staged`

## Deployment Process

### Cloudflare Workers (frontend SPA)
- **SSOT:** `documentation/DOC_CLOUDFLARE_WORKERS.md` + `wrangler.jsonc`
- Push-to-deploy via Workers Builds; which branch is staging vs production: `git-workflow/RULE.mdc` § Mode behavior table → **staging** / **production** (SSOT for setup: `documentation/DOC_CLOUDFLARE_WORKERS.md`)

### Cloud Functions Deployment
- Deploy yourself when changes require it; verify success
- **SSOT:** `cloud-functions/RULE.mdc` — deploy commands, lint, Supabase Edge workflow

